    <heading level="1">Everyday Math</heading>
    <exercise number="273" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Landscaping Sue and Alan are planning to put a 15 foot square swimming pool in their backyard. They will surround the pool with a tiled deck, the same width on all sides. If the width of the deck is w, the total area of the pool and deck is given by the trinomial $$4w^{2} + 60w + 225$$ . Factor the trinomial.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( 2 w + 15 ) 2 ( 2 w + 15 ) 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="274" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Home repair The height a twelve foot ladder can reach up the side of a building if the ladder’s base is b feet from the building is the square root of the binomial $$144 - b^{2}$$ . Factor the binomial.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
